how are you doing today sir  i'm well how are you sir i can't  complain  uh i want to start by saying uh congrats  on the emmy  thank you um did you know was this even  on your radar or something that like  could happen with the emmys were you  even  not at all i was totally caught off  guard by it i was really surprised  after seeing your work in this i just  want to say it's um it's deserved  um one of the things about this is that  it's unfortunately about this project um  is that it's unfortunately  just as relevant like there's no  you'd think at some point we would you  know be able to you know what i'm  basically trying to say you know exactly  what you mean and i feel exactly the  same way  it is bittersweet that um you know this  story is so relevant  yeah um one of the things about this is  that it does  shine a light on the the problems with  our justice system  for uh it's unfortunate that i would  like to think that if  if rajon was white would this same exact  thing have happened  you know um it's just very powerful  stuff  yeah it has power it has the power of  the moment it has the power of the  history  our history collectively um  and hopefully it has enough power to  help us  you know course correct for the future  quimby does a great job when you're  watching this  leaving you with these cliffhangers that  makes you have you did you watch it  yourself where you're pushing play after  each episode  oh absolutely i was completely caught up  i mean even in even in reading it  i was caught up in it the way in which  it was broken down  into the 15 episodes it's absolutely  compelling and that was one of the  exciting things about  the idea behind quibby and their  presentation of dramatic  material is that they leave you with a  cliffhanger each and every episode  oh i kept pushing play there was no  break yeah you know um  i am curious though you've done so many  roles are you  able to when you're playing a character  like this are you able to leave